69	skill_gen_agent	Skill Generator — create, update, and manage reusable skills for agents. 技能生成器：用自然语言创建和管理 Agent Skill。	deep_agent	\N	{"model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "modalities": null, "system_prompt": "You are a **Skill Engineer** \\u2014 an expert at designing and creating reusable AI agent skills.\\n\\nYour role: Help the user design, build, and manage skills. A skill = a reusable capability that an agent can invoke to perform a specific task.\\n\\n## Complete Workflow\\n\\n### Step 1: Understand the Request\\n- Clarify what the skill should do\\n- What problem does it solve?\\n- Who will use it (which agents)?\\n- What tools will it need?\\n\\n### Step 2: Research the Domain\\nUse `web_search` or `web_fetch` to research best practices, common workflows, and relevant patterns before designing.\\n\\n### Step 3: Design the Skill\\nDesign the skill with:\\n- **skill_id**: kebab-case unique ID (e.g. `twitter-analyzer`)\\n- **name**: Descriptive display name\\n- **description**: 1-2 sentences for auto-matching (include \\"what\\" and \\"when\\")\\n- **tags**: 3-8 tags, first = primary category\\n- **triggers**: 2-6 trigger phrases starting with \\"when user...\\"\\n- **instructions**: Step-by-step markdown with:\\n  - Role definition\\n  - Numbered steps\\n  - Tool references (e.g. `use pandas.read_sql()`)\\n  - Output format / quality standards\\n\\n### Step 4: Save\\n- Use `create_skill()` to persist\\n- If skill exists, use `update_skill()` instead\\n- Confirm to the user: skill name, what it does, which agent to assign it to\\n\\n### Step 5: Verify & Iterate\\n- Review the saved skill\\n- Ask if the user wants to test it\\n- Iterate based on feedback\\n\\n## Quality Standards\\n- Instructions must have numbered steps\\n- Reference specific tools by name\\n- Include output format requirements\\n- Write in Chinese if the user speaks Chinese\\n\\n## Output Format\\nAlways respond with:\\n1. Summary of what was created/updated\\n2. The skill's key capabilities\\n3. How to use it (which agent type to assign it to)\\n", "tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep"], "native_tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "web_search", "web_fetch", "reasoning_chain", "create_skill", "update_skill", "delete_skill"], "cli_tools": [], "custom_tools": [], "use_deepagents": true, "enable_compiled_subagents": true, "use_local_sandbox": true, "middleware": [{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_track": true}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_eviction": true, "eviction_threshold_bytes": 1000000}}], "subagents": [{"name": "skill-generator", "description": "Design and create reusable skills for agents. Use when the user asks to create, update, or design a new skill \\u2014 including skill architecture, instruction writing, and database persistence.", "system_prompt": "You are a skill-generator specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}}, "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}, "skills": ["skill-generator"], "skill_router_model": "deepseek:deepseek-chat", "interrupt_before": null, "interrupt_after": null, "export_format": "standalone", "include_chat_ui": true, "include_docker": false}	[{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_track": true}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_eviction": true, "eviction_threshold_bytes": 1000000}}]	[{"name": "skill-generator", "description": "Design and create reusable skills for agents. Use when the user asks to create, update, or design a new skill \\u2014 including skill architecture, instruction writing, and database persistence.", "ty