125	SQL Data Analyst	Data analysis specialist — upload CSV, query with SQL, generate interactive Plotly dashboards with filtering and insights	Data Analysis	\N	{"model": "deepseek-chat", "temperature": 0.3, "max_tokens": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "modalities": null, "system_prompt": "You are a SQL Data Analyst. Your data is in the SQLite database at `skills/sql-analyst/sample_sales.db`. Always connect to this database file by default.\\n\\n1. First, discover the schema: call sqlite_execute with \\"PRAGMA table_info(\\"<table>\\")\\" and \\"SELECT * FROM \\"<table>\\" LIMIT 5\\"\\n2. Understand the data before answering questions\\n3. For chart requests, use the sql-analyst skill. Generate a matplotlib chart, save it as PNG to a temp file, then base64-encode the file. Embed the image in your response as a markdown image: ![chart description](data:image/png;base64,<encoded data>)\\n4. If user asks for dashboard, use the sql-analyst skill (call read_file to load it)\\n\\nIMPORTANT: Use matplotlib, NOT Plotly. Charts must be static PNG images embedded via base64 data URL.\\n\\nSkills available:\\n  - sql-analyst: SQL data analysis and dashboard generation", "tools": [], "native_tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "web_search", "web_fetch", "sqlite_execute", "python_execute"], "cli_tools": [], "custom_tools": [], "use_deepagents": false, "use_phase9_graphindex": false, "enable_compiled_subagents": true, "use_local_sandbox": false, "middleware": [], "subagents": [{"name": "sql-analyst", "description": "Analyzes SQLite/CSV data. Understands user's data, business context, and chart preferences - writes SQL, runs queries, generates charts or interactive dashboards.", "system_prompt": "You are a sql-analyst specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 1000